 ## 🚀 Complete Deployment Guide
 
-This guide shows how to deploy Grubify with **both backend versions** (v1 with memory leak, v2 with payment failures) for testing Azure SRE Agent scenarios.
+The current v1 source removes the unbounded 10 MB-per-request analytics cache.
+The historical v1 image can still reproduce the memory-leak lab, while v2
+intentionally simulates payment failures. Use `API_VERSION=v1` for the working demo.
+
+### Regression checks
+
+Orders use catalog prices and the same rounded 8% tax and flat $2.99 delivery fee
+as the cart. Checkout preserves the phone number and restaurant details. Delivery
+estimates use the longest item preparation time plus 15 minutes. Cancellation is
+available before preparation starts and is not undone by the demo's status timer.
+`/health` provides the API liveness endpoint.
+
+```powershell
+# From this directory, against a disposable/test deployment:
+.\scripts\verify-app.ps1 -BaseUrl https://YOUR-API-HOST
+
+Set-Location .\grubify-frontend
+$env:CI = 'true'
+npm test -- --watchAll=false --runInBand
+npm run build
+```
+
+The API check creates an isolated test cart and cancelled order, performs 150 cart
+requests, verifies totals, tracking, validation and cancellation, then clears the
+test cart. Run it with a single API replica: carts and orders are demo-only,
+in-memory state and do not survive restarts or replicate across instances.
+Payments remain simulated; this is not a production payment system.
 
